{"availability":"available","full":"jeannesbryan/phosphor","name":"phosphor","description":"Phosphor is a lightweight, cyberpunk-terminal-styled Nostr web client built on the KISS principle. Features offline-first local caching, multi-media uploads, Proof-of-Work mining, long-form articles, sport activity tracking, ephemeral stories, and multi-relay support.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-12T18:28:24Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:51:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://phosphor-nostr.pages.dev","topics":["activity-tracking","blossom","cyberpunk","cyberpunk-ui","decentralization","indexeddb","nostr","nostr-client","nostr-protocol","proof-of-work","pwa","terminal-ui","vanilla-js"],"demo":"https://phosphor-nostr.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.354Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.354Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.354Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.354Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Phosphor is a Nostr web client built on the KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid) principle, wrapped in a thick cyberpunk-terminal aesthetic. It is specifically designed for a lightweight, instant reading and interaction experience on the Nostr network without the bloat of modern interfaces.","This client UI is built entirely on top of the Terminal Framework created by @jeannesbryan."],"features":["Minimalist Timeline: Fetch Text Note feeds (NIP-01) in real-time without lag.","Timeline Tabs & Filtering: Toggle seamlessly between a curated Following timeline (instantly filtered via lightweight CSS selectors based on your Kind 3 follow list) and a live Global stream.","Aggressive Local Caching: Utilizes IndexedDB to cache user profiles locally, drastically reducing redundant relay queries and providing instant timeline rendering.","Proof of Work (NIP-13): Native support for adjusting computational difficulty (up to Level 16) directly from the composer to prevent network spam, utilizing an asynchronous event loop that doesn't freeze your browser.","Notifications & Mentions: Dedicated hub to monitor network signals, replies, mentions, reposts, and telemetry reactions targeting your node."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeannesbryan/phosphor/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"7f76718ca5664a534bade2b2ddb6c6ca8158b2347e14ff3dce6455f322044d03","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.569Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.569Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Phosphor is a Nostr web client built on the KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid) principle, wrapped in a thick cyberpunk-terminal aesthetic. It is specifically designed for a lightweight, instant reading and interaction experience on the Nostr network without the bloat of modern interfaces.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeannesbryan/phosphor/blob/main/readme.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Phosphor is a Nostr web client built on the KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid) principle, wrapped in a thick cyberpunk-terminal aesthetic. It is specifically designed for a lightweight, instant reading and interaction experience on the Nostr network without the bloat of modern interfaces.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeannesbryan/phosphor/blob/main/readme.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Nomadic Network Preferences (NIP-65): Automatically syncs and applies your custom relay network topology (Kind 10002) upon login, overriding static configurations for true portability.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeannesbryan/phosphor/blob/main/readme.md"}],"fingerprint":"7f76718ca5664a534bade2b2ddb6c6ca8158b2347e14ff3dce6455f322044d03","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeannesbryan/phosphor/blob/main/readme.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:05.569Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T05:51:17Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeanne